-    After /clear or /compact: knowledge base preserved. Tell user: "context-mode knowledge base preserved. Use \`ctx purge\` to start fresh."
-  </ctx_commands>
-` : ''}
+  Tool output stays in your context for the whole session. When you intend to PROCESS output (filter, count, parse, aggregate), do it in the sandbox and print only the answer:
+  - ${t("ctx_batch_execute")}(commands, queries): run several commands, index their output, search it in one call.
+  - ${t("ctx_execute")}(language, code) | ${t("ctx_execute_file")}(path, language, code): only what the code prints comes back.
+  - ${t("ctx_search")}(queries): search indexed output and auto-captured session memory (sort: "timeline" after a resume or compaction).
+  - ${t("ctx_fetch_and_index")}(url, source) instead of WebFetch.
